SYNTHESIS
  Relation-code features are real signal but not a replacement for
  generated-word compatibility.  Globally A3/A4/dmin correlate strongly
  with q0, U4, and B2, but that is partly a size effect.  Within fixed
  shape size, the signs are mixed, and size=3 has the worst q0/U4
  witnesses while the simple |coef|<=2 relation spectrum is flat.
  Therefore the proof stack should stay sequential:
    generated miss-zeta death-chain/context-merge compatibility first;
    relation-code A3/MDS packet selection second;
    factorial q0/Vitali atom boundary evaluation last.
  The useful theorem target is not 'A3 implies compatibility'.  It is
  'compatibility reduces surviving packets to a low-support relation
  ledger whose leading finite cases are organized by A3/dmin/MDS'.
